WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:03.294
[screaming]

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.587
It's a little over the top,

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:07.632
but I think it depicts a time in the mob

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:10.593
when they had power like
that to send a message.

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:12.262
Hello, my name is John Pennisi.

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:15.265
I'm a former made member of
the Lucchese crime family.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:19.477
I also got involved as a low associate

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.980
to the Gambino family
when I was very young.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.441
Today, we're going to be
looking at Mafia scenes

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:25.608
in movies and TV,

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:28.028
and we're going to
judge how real they are.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.237
All right.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:34.159
He sat on one [bleep] the whole way over!

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:35.201
[laughing]

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.370
And what's depicted here is a guy getting

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.790
what we would call
straightened out, inducted.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:45.211
And it's inaccurate by the way
that they're kidding around.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.338
This is a serious ceremony

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:50.133
where there's no joking or playing around.

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:53.011
OK.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:56.222
That's St. Peter, my family saint.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.725
Now, as that card burns, so
may your soul burn in hell

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.852
if you betray your friends in the family.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.771
There was two members being made,

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:04.355
and that is not accurate.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:05.815
It would be one at a time.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:08.943
They would bring one
person up into the room

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:11.780
and do the ceremony and
then call the other one up.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.158
Some of the things were
accurate that were said,

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:17.410
and obviously the pricking of the finger

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.495
and the burning of the saint,

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:22.582
but all in all, it wasn't 100%.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.673
I don't know if they put
it there for this reason,

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:33.718
but a lot of Italians are
superstitious about birds.

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:37.222
They don't even give cards
out with birds on it.

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:39.099
They don't think it's a good sign.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.391
You've been doing really good this year

00:01:40.391 --> 00:01:41.643
with the sports book.

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:42.977
Yeah, it's been good.

00:01:42.977 --> 00:01:45.271
I'm going to give it to
you, my boy. It's yours.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.398
Nothing's set in stone

00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:51.027
of how long you have to go as an associate

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:52.862
before you become an inducted member.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:56.032
Some people have been
associates for 10, 15 years,

00:01:56.032 --> 00:01:57.784
five years, 10 years, three years.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:01.162
When I first got
straightened out, it was the,

00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:04.624
at that time, the highest honor

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:08.128
to be inducted into a family
and to become a wise guy

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.963
and to be treated with that respect.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.257
Looking back on it now,

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:15.218
it was the lowest point of my life.

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:17.262
It was an embarrassment,

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:19.973
because basically everything

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:23.059
that I thought the life was about

00:02:23.059 --> 00:02:24.352
was a farce.

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:26.896
From a scale from 1 to
10, I'd rate it a 3.

00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:29.732
Listen to me, Michael.

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:30.775
Know who your friends are.

00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:32.068
We've been together 40 years.

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:35.029
Passing around jewelry,
and — that's insane.

00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:38.116
I don't even, I couldn't even
answer what that is about

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:39.742
and why they would put
something like that.

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:42.996
We want to do business with you, Michael.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.038
We've been together too many years.

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:45.498
We can wash our money.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:49.502
This was a commission meeting
with the heads of families.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.297
New York is chopped up
by the five families,

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:55.383
and everybody knows their
place, and they know who's who.

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.093
The commission would meet

00:02:57.093 --> 00:03:01.181
if there was business to
discuss within the families

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.057
and decisions to be made.

00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:04.684
Only the people involved in the meeting

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.352
would obviously be in the know

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.605
of where and when and what
time they were meeting.

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:12.233
They could take an
underboss or consigliere,

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:14.152
or even a captain if they want.

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.778
The different families intermingle

00:03:15.778 --> 00:03:17.864
a lot more than people understand,

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:21.159
and it's not so territorial
as people think.

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.827
[glass breaking]
[guns firing]

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:24.871
[helicopter blades whirring]

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.289
[gun firing]

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:28.917
If they were attempting to hit somebody,

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:32.378
it would definitely not be that flashy.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.922
It was very Hollywood to me,

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:37.008
with the helicopter and the machine guns.

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:38.301
This would never happen.

00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:43.097
It would be very low-key
and be done quietly.

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:47.268
On a scale of 1 to 10,
I would rate this a 0.

00:03:47.268 --> 00:03:50.271
We're going to try you out
with a little delivery job.

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:53.483
It's for a, uh, private
lottery that we run.

00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:55.443
The mob is always testing you.

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:58.071
They may give you something
to do or an assignment,

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.698
and they want to see how
well you do and carry it out.

00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:03.660
That would be to just see
how you perform overall

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.411
and that you stand up

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.497
and that you do what you're told to do.

00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:09.249
There was a saying in the mob

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.918
that there was no rule book given out,

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.629
and you had to pick
these things up yourself,

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:17.465
growing up and being around the life.

00:04:17.465 --> 00:04:18.258
Gotcha!

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:20.218
What seems to be the problem, officers?

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:21.261
Was I speeding?

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.138
We'll decide what you were
doing after an illegal search.

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:27.517
In that life, you should always assume

00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:31.437
that you're being watched
and followed and surveilled.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.897
That's the FBI's job.

00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:37.277
The FBI is out there doing
their job, trying to make cases,

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.445
so you should always assume

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.364
that they are out there watching you.

00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:43.449
Some people may call it paranoia.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.285
I call it self-preservation.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.244
First and foremost,

00:04:46.244 --> 00:04:49.622
you shouldn't talk on
the phone at any time.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.624
And you should just watch who you talk to,

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.501
be very careful who you're speaking to

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:54.877
and what you're speaking about.

00:04:54.877 --> 00:04:57.630
Most things are done and
should be done in person,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.841
and you should also be leery of new people

00:04:59.841 --> 00:05:00.842
that you're meeting.

00:05:00.842 --> 00:05:03.052
I'd rather plan some felonies.

00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:05.930
Oh. Then we should meet at
our Mafia crime headquarters.

00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:11.185
I think years ago, they
used to have storefronts

00:05:11.185 --> 00:05:14.022
and then the back would be a club

00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:15.940
or a place where they would gather,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.192
more so then than now.

00:05:18.192 --> 00:05:21.571
Meetings today would take
place in a restaurant.

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:24.157
In our case, it was a cigar lounge.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:27.035
Or at someone's house or even outside.

00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:30.538
I beg you, I can't make
this week's loan payment.

00:05:30.538 --> 00:05:34.751
Look into your hard drive
and open your mercy file!

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:37.211
File not found.

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:40.506
Loan-sharking is a big part
of the income of the mob.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.134
Money would be lent to anyone.

00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:45.261
You know, people in
desperate need of money,

00:05:45.261 --> 00:05:46.971
businessmen, anyone.

00:05:46.971 --> 00:05:48.598
Ooh, this guy's an ox.

00:05:48.598 --> 00:05:50.475
He's got oxen-like strength.

00:05:50.475 --> 00:05:52.393
Hey, he needs a nickname, right?

00:05:52.393 --> 00:05:53.978
Let's call him Clamps.

00:05:53.978 --> 00:05:55.772
I myself didn't have a nickname.

00:05:55.772 --> 00:05:57.815
There's names like Johnny Sideburns

00:05:57.815 --> 00:05:59.275
that I speak about a lot.

00:05:59.275 --> 00:06:02.445
Guys have names like Sammy
Meatball, Sammy Clams,

00:06:02.445 --> 00:06:06.115
and it depends. Sometimes
it's an attribute to you.

00:06:06.115 --> 00:06:08.951
I'm going to rate it, based on the future,

00:06:08.951 --> 00:06:10.495
I'll give it a 1.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.333
[screaming]

00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:17.627
I remember seeing "The
Godfather" when I was younger.

00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:20.171
But I was very young and not in the life.

00:06:20.171 --> 00:06:22.924
I think that a lot of young
guys who watched "The Godfather"

00:06:22.924 --> 00:06:25.593
all wanted to be gangsters
after watching it.

00:06:25.593 --> 00:06:27.011
It's a little over the top,

00:06:27.011 --> 00:06:30.014
but I think it depicts a time in the mob

00:06:30.014 --> 00:06:32.850
when they had power like
that to send a message.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.645
There were some forms of
intimidation, verbally,

00:06:35.645 --> 00:06:38.856
that people would give
out or send a message.

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:42.902
At times, people could
get a beating from the mob

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.446
or get their windows broken or something,

00:06:45.446 --> 00:06:48.866
some kind of sign to tell
the person, you know,

00:06:48.866 --> 00:06:50.827
that they're not happy about something.

00:06:50.827 --> 00:06:52.453
Being that it's "The Godfather,"

00:06:52.453 --> 00:06:56.124
I will rate this at a 7.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:57.792
Our mole with the Russians

00:06:57.792 --> 00:07:00.086
tells things a little different.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:02.046
That's a [bleep] lie!

00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:04.132
If you're being questioned
about something,

00:07:04.132 --> 00:07:05.967
they already know you're guilty of it.

00:07:05.967 --> 00:07:07.510
As far as punishment goes,

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:11.013
it could go from someone
getting a tongue lashing

00:07:11.013 --> 00:07:12.432
to them losing their life.

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.809
People in that life always
make a lot of mistakes,

00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:17.562
so there's always
something that you hear of.

00:07:17.562 --> 00:07:19.105
Someone's always in trouble.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.607
Most of the time you would
hear something internally,

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.901
but sometimes you would
hear about somebody

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:26.404
that made a mistake in another family.

00:07:26.404 --> 00:07:28.322
Now, my son is waiting
out there in the car

00:07:28.322 --> 00:07:29.824
to go to the movies,

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:31.117
and I ain't going to disappoint him.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:33.661
[muffled screaming]

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.498
So, most of us would try

00:07:37.498 --> 00:07:39.625
to keep our personal lives personal,

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:42.462
away from that life that we lived.

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:45.006
I believe most families assume

00:07:45.006 --> 00:07:47.383
what the person is doing with their life,

00:07:47.383 --> 00:07:49.635
but it shouldn't be talked
about with your family.

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:52.430
Some family members are
definitely completely in the dark

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:55.016
about what their either husband or father

00:07:55.016 --> 00:07:57.810
or brother or son are doing.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.604
As this whole thing unfolded

00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:02.398
from the beginning to where I am today,

00:08:02.398 --> 00:08:04.108
had a big effect on my family.

00:08:04.108 --> 00:08:06.944
I don't get to see them
as often as I like to.

00:08:06.944 --> 00:08:08.905
They have to go through it with me,

00:08:08.905 --> 00:08:12.408
and it's unfortunate, and they suffer too.

00:08:12.408 --> 00:08:16.579
On a scale of 1 to 10, I
would rate this another 0.

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:18.456
He says, "I must be dreaming."

00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:20.833
[laughing]

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:25.171
Travolta tried his best
to play John Gotti.

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.673
I don't think that really
anyone can play him.

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:29.884
Although the makeup artist had him

00:08:29.884 --> 00:08:31.302
look like John Gotti a little bit.

00:08:31.302 --> 00:08:33.221
He tried to get the New York accent right,

00:08:33.221 --> 00:08:34.972
but it wasn't 100%.

00:08:34.972 --> 00:08:36.891
John Gotti was a caporegime,

00:08:36.891 --> 00:08:40.645
which is a captain in the
family during this time.

00:08:40.645 --> 00:08:43.898
I had gotten to meet him
twice, with his son, John Jr.

00:08:43.898 --> 00:08:46.150
Once in Regine's in Manhattan,

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:49.695
second time at a club that
they had in Ozone Park.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:52.740
The job now is to maintain
continuity of leadership.

00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:55.034
So,

00:08:56.744 --> 00:09:00.456
I nominate John Gotti.

00:09:00.456 --> 00:09:02.291
So, this scene was depicted

00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:05.503
obviously after Paul
Castellano gets killed

00:09:05.503 --> 00:09:09.048
and the family has to
put in place a new boss.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:12.843
This scene would depict probably

00:09:12.843 --> 00:09:14.679
part of the administration

00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.389
and captains in the family,

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:20.184
the administration being
boss, underboss, consigliere.

00:09:20.184 --> 00:09:24.313
Obviously in this scene,
the boss is no longer alive.

00:09:24.313 --> 00:09:25.940
I believe it to be pretty accurate.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.775
I think that they would nominate,

00:09:27.775 --> 00:09:29.443
as they did, John Gotti,

00:09:29.443 --> 00:09:32.572
and they would not
necessarily take a vote,

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:36.117
but no one would oppose it.

00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:37.952
I second the motion.

00:09:41.539 --> 00:09:44.292
[clapping]

00:09:44.292 --> 00:09:48.754
So, after he's voted in as
boss of the Gambino family,

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:50.006
it just goes to show you

00:09:50.006 --> 00:09:52.550
that you don't have to have the last name.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.969
That name came from Carlo Gambino,

00:09:54.969 --> 00:09:58.556
and it was passed down to Paul Castellano

00:09:58.556 --> 00:10:00.766
and then taken over by John Gotti.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:02.893
Paul Castellano was put in the position

00:10:02.893 --> 00:10:05.563
because he was related to Carlo Gambino,

00:10:05.563 --> 00:10:07.648
but he was a businessman.

00:10:07.648 --> 00:10:10.067
John Gotti took the position

00:10:10.067 --> 00:10:12.778
from being a gangster, street guy.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.614
Two different kinds of bosses.

00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:17.825
I think as a good boss,
you need brains and brawn.

00:10:17.825 --> 00:10:20.828
So you need to be smart business-wise,

00:10:20.828 --> 00:10:22.079
and you need to be a gangster,

00:10:22.079 --> 00:10:23.331
a tough guy in the street.

00:10:23.331 --> 00:10:25.291
I would rate this scene an 8.

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:28.252
Where you at? I got a lot of money here.

00:10:28.252 --> 00:10:29.837
Let's play cards.

00:10:31.547 --> 00:10:32.757
Guys like to play cards.

00:10:32.757 --> 00:10:36.927
Card games that I'd seen was
in cafés and things like that.

00:10:36.927 --> 00:10:37.762
Not like that.

00:10:38.929 --> 00:10:40.306
I got your message, Arty.

00:10:40.306 --> 00:10:43.476
From here on, nothing goes
down unless I'm involved.

00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:45.936
No blackjack, no dope deals, no nothing.

00:10:45.936 --> 00:10:49.065
A nickel bag gets sold
in the park, I want in.

00:10:49.065 --> 00:10:51.984
If the mob was going to
deal with a drug dealer,

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:55.529
a known drug dealer, it
would more be on the sneak

00:10:55.529 --> 00:10:57.573
and very low-key and quiet.

00:10:57.573 --> 00:10:59.825
It wouldn't be coming into
social clubs like that.

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:01.369
It would have to be done on the sneak

00:11:01.369 --> 00:11:03.496
because there was a rule

00:11:03.496 --> 00:11:05.373
that there's no drug dealing in that life.

00:11:05.373 --> 00:11:08.000
So that's a rule that's often broken.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.710
The other rule, that you're not to go

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:13.005
with a made member's wife or girl,

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:15.174
is broke all the time.

00:11:15.174 --> 00:11:16.217
You think you're going to live long enough

00:11:16.217 --> 00:11:18.969
to spend that money, you [bleep] hump?

00:11:20.429 --> 00:11:21.889
[gun firing]

00:11:21.889 --> 00:11:25.685
I think the violence, all
the way up till the '90s,

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:28.562
was at a high as compared to today,

00:11:28.562 --> 00:11:31.190
and that's because of the cameras

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.484
and cellphones and technology,

00:11:33.484 --> 00:11:37.988
so the violence has been more low-key.

00:11:37.988 --> 00:11:39.615
I would rate this a 2.

00:11:39.615 --> 00:11:41.742
You will be hearing from me, Mr. Scott.

00:11:41.742 --> 00:11:42.618
OK, well.

00:11:42.618 --> 00:11:44.745
I can be very, very persistent.

00:11:44.745 --> 00:11:45.955
Do your worst.

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:49.500
Most likely the guy that
was selling insurance

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.336
was just trying to portray
himself as a street guy.

00:11:52.336 --> 00:11:54.255
He definitely wasn't what we would call

00:11:54.255 --> 00:11:57.091
a friend in the street, selling insurance.

00:11:57.091 --> 00:11:58.718
All mobsters have a front.

00:11:58.718 --> 00:12:00.511
Sometimes it's selling insurance,

00:12:00.511 --> 00:12:03.347
sometimes it's waste
management or sanitation.

00:12:03.347 --> 00:12:05.474
For the record, not all Italian Americans

00:12:05.474 --> 00:12:07.017
are in the Mafia.

00:12:07.017 --> 00:12:10.479
The legitimate businesses
that they get into varies,

00:12:10.479 --> 00:12:12.898
and it's really what fits that person.

00:12:12.898 --> 00:12:15.443
They get involved in a lot
of legitimate businesses.

00:12:15.443 --> 00:12:16.986
It is a front,

00:12:16.986 --> 00:12:20.239
and it's to kind of throw
law enforcement off too

00:12:20.239 --> 00:12:22.241
as to where they're
getting their money from.

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:25.327
I would say 90% of the people
in the life are Italian,

00:12:25.327 --> 00:12:28.998
and then you would have probably
10% who are non-Italians,

00:12:28.998 --> 00:12:30.708
and they're just associates.

00:12:30.708 --> 00:12:32.710
I would rate this scene as a 5.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.044
I want to go to college.

00:12:34.044 --> 00:12:36.255
I can't get caught with [bleep] like this.

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:37.965
Look, you take the speakers, right?

00:12:37.965 --> 00:12:39.759
At the same time, you say to yourself,

00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:42.595
"This is the last time I'm
ever gonna steal something."

00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:44.555
It's that simple.

00:12:44.555 --> 00:12:49.059
It's a low-level thing
that he's involved in,

00:12:49.059 --> 00:12:51.520
but he would gradually graduate

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.773
to more sophisticated crimes.

00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:55.900
You start hanging around with people

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:58.694
who bring you around
someone that's involved,

00:12:58.694 --> 00:13:00.696
usually on the outskirts,

00:13:00.696 --> 00:13:03.449
and eventually you'll become an associate

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:04.784
if they want you to.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:07.870
But for the most part, it's being young

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:11.874
and easily influenced by these older guys.

00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:14.460
That's what drew me to the life,

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:17.755
being part of this group
of well-respected men.

00:13:17.755 --> 00:13:21.217
That is the allure of
getting involved in our life.

00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:22.551
You don't pick that life.

00:13:22.551 --> 00:13:24.220
I always say that life picks you.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.096
I would give this scene a 5.

00:13:26.096 --> 00:13:28.599
A young guy just don't
wake up one day and say,

00:13:28.599 --> 00:13:30.017
"Hey, I'm gonna join the mob."

00:13:30.017 --> 00:13:33.604
By circumstance, you may know
somebody who knows somebody,

00:13:33.604 --> 00:13:35.272
and that's usually the way it goes.

00:13:35.272 --> 00:13:37.817
As a young man growing
up in both Ozone Park

00:13:37.817 --> 00:13:42.321
and Howard Beach, Queens,
the mob was always around,

00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:44.240
and I kind of got involved

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:47.701
as a low associate

00:13:47.701 --> 00:13:50.496
to the Gambino family
when I was very young.

00:13:50.496 --> 00:13:52.331
But by the age of 19,

00:13:52.331 --> 00:13:55.960
I'd wind up getting myself
in a lot of trouble.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.629
I did 17 years in prison.

00:13:58.629 --> 00:14:00.714
I kind of stood away from the street

00:14:00.714 --> 00:14:03.801
for various reasons for about five years

00:14:03.801 --> 00:14:06.053
and then was pulled back into the street,

00:14:06.053 --> 00:14:09.056
and I'd wind up becoming affiliated

00:14:09.056 --> 00:14:12.101
to the Lucchese family at that point.

00:14:12.101 --> 00:14:14.603
And I became a Lucchese associate,

00:14:14.603 --> 00:14:18.649
and I went on to become an
inducted member inside of a year.

00:14:18.649 --> 00:14:22.528
I was inducted into the life in 2013,

00:14:22.528 --> 00:14:24.446
and I left in 2018.

00:14:24.446 --> 00:14:28.367
So, I was falsely accused
of cooperating on a case

00:14:28.367 --> 00:14:30.202
that just happened within our family.

00:14:30.202 --> 00:14:31.537
And I know there's no such thing

00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:33.038
as walking away from the mob,

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:34.790
but I basically just wanted

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:38.210
to just try to live my life in peace.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.838
They would not stop hunting me down,

00:14:40.838 --> 00:14:43.090
sending people to come after me,

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:45.885
and that was the deciding factor

00:14:45.885 --> 00:14:48.512
in my going to the government

00:14:48.512 --> 00:14:50.598
and cooperating with the government.

00:14:50.598 --> 00:14:54.518
Here is a list of every known
member in organized crime,

00:14:54.518 --> 00:14:57.521
according to the FBI,
that you cannot talk to,

00:14:57.521 --> 00:15:01.692
meet, associate with,
come in contact with.

00:15:01.692 --> 00:15:04.904
This character is obviously out on parole,

00:15:04.904 --> 00:15:06.739
or on paper, as we say,

00:15:06.739 --> 00:15:09.867
and his lawyer's advising
him of his stipulations

00:15:09.867 --> 00:15:11.493
that he has to follow,

00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:13.704
and some of those stipulations are

00:15:13.704 --> 00:15:17.458
not associating with anyone
known in organized crime

00:15:17.458 --> 00:15:21.086
or anyone with a conviction.

00:15:21.086 --> 00:15:22.755
I mean, guys don't want
to be in the life today.

00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:23.923
Are you [bleep] nuts?

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:26.717
They get locked up and
arrested within three years.

00:15:26.717 --> 00:15:29.929
10 guys get pinched, nine
guys want to cooperate.

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:33.265
It's a [bleep] race to
the government's doorstep.

00:15:33.265 --> 00:15:36.602
When a pinch comes down,
which means an arrest,

00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:39.897
10 guys get pinched, nine guys flip.

00:15:39.897 --> 00:15:41.357
That may be a little high,

00:15:41.357 --> 00:15:45.027
but it's pretty accurate that
a lot of guys turn quickly.

00:15:45.027 --> 00:15:47.237
They want to avoid going to jail.

00:15:47.237 --> 00:15:50.449
The movie and TV depicts Mafia members

00:15:50.449 --> 00:15:53.661
as being honorable, loyal, and respectful.

00:15:53.661 --> 00:15:55.579
And it's a myth.

00:15:55.579 --> 00:15:57.206
There is no loyalty,

00:15:57.206 --> 00:15:58.916
there is no honor,

00:15:58.916 --> 00:16:00.084
there's none of that.

00:16:00.084 --> 00:16:03.587
In today's times, all
that has been replaced

00:16:03.587 --> 00:16:05.631
by selfishness and greed,

00:16:05.631 --> 00:16:07.383
and people have a misconception

00:16:07.383 --> 00:16:08.801
of really what it's about.

00:16:08.801 --> 00:16:11.595
I would give this scene a 10.

00:16:11.595 --> 00:16:14.765
I created a blog. It's
called Sitdown News,

00:16:14.765 --> 00:16:18.727
and I basically cover most mob stories.

00:16:18.727 --> 00:16:22.773
And created a podcast called
"The MBA and the Button Man."

00:16:22.773 --> 00:16:24.483
I want to thank everyone for watching,

00:16:24.483 --> 00:16:27.069
and if you enjoyed the video,
please click the link above.

